---
// src/components/portableText/PortableTextUnknownMark.astro
//
// Renders whatever text a mark reference resolves to, no wrapper
// element at all. Exists for one specific, confirmed data shape: a
// handful of migrated WordPress posts have a span whose `marks` array
// references a markDef _key that isn't actually present in that
// block's own markDefs (found via a full production build -- e.g.
// turfrx-oxycal-why-when-and-how's h3 headings reference a link markDef
// that's missing, while the identical text elsewhere in the same post
// *is* correctly linked -- a migration-script artifact, not a schema
// gap or anything a future editor's content can trigger the same way).
//
// Without this, astro-portabletext's default fallback still renders
// the text (so nothing was ever visually broken/missing), but wraps it
// in `<span data-portabletext-unknown="mark">` and logs a console
// warning on every build. This is strictly about that cosmetic/log
// cleanup -- see src/lib/portableTextComponents.ts's comment for the
// separate, actual content fix (restoring the missing links) that's
// been flagged rather than done here, since guessing at the intended
// href isn't a code change.

---
<slot />
